---
title: Quiche
description: A classic Quiche Lorraine with a buttery pâte brisée crust, silky egg custard, bacon, leeks, and Gruyere.
course: main
cuisine: French
servings: 12
time required: 5 hours
prep time: 3 hours
cook time: 1 hour 30 minutes
source: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8vKcUj_kiYI
image: https://static.cordonbleu.edu/Files/MediaFile/61129.jpg
tags:
  - quiche
  - eggs
  - bacon
  - french
  - brunch
  - pastry
---

Make the short-crust dough (pâte brisée). Chill the dry ingredients, bowl, and paddle in the freezer for ~20 minutes, and keep the ice water cold in the fridge. Mix @unsalted butter{205%g} and @bread flour{250%g} on low speed until it looks like coarse sand with a few medium clumps, about ~5-10 minutes. Add @kosher salt{3%g} along the way.

Add the @ice water{1/4%cup} and mix until a smooth ball forms. Shape into a puck on a floured surface, wrap in plastic, and refrigerate at least ~2 hours (overnight is better).

Roll the dough straight from the fridge to about 1/8 inch thick. Lay it over your #pie dish{} and gently press it into the mold, then trim the excess. Chill again for ~30 minutes.

Blind bake the crust in a #oven{} at 400°F for ~25-30 minutes, then remove the foil and bake another ~5-10 minutes until golden.

Make the egg base. Blend @eggs{11}, @whole milk{260%g}, @heavy cream{260%g}, and @kosher salt{15%g} with an #immersion blender{}, avoiding incorporating too much air.

Cook the @bacon{6%slices}(thick-cut, chopped) until crisp-tender, then drain. Thinly slice the @onion{1} and @leeks{2}.

Layer the bacon, onion, and leeks into the pre-baked crust, then add the @gruyere cheese{150%g}(cubed or shredded). Sprinkle over the @fresh thyme{2%sprigs}(leaves picked), a few microplane passes of @nutmeg{1%g}, and @black pepper{} to taste. Pour the egg base over the top.

Bake at 350°F for ~40-60 minutes until just set and barely jiggly in the middle.

Rest the quiche at least ~25 minutes before slicing. Remove it from the mold and let it cool another ~10 minutes, then slice into portions and serve.
